n  made for instance by Italian authorities  in the Italian hotspot or by Greek  authorities in the Greek hotspot but we  can also support other member states and  for instance I can report that we have  now a very good an extensive intensive  cooperation with Germany and there we we  see that we we support also Germany with  with the return operations mr. lazarey  I'd like to ask you about the the front  tax efforts at sea in the Mediterranean  are you going to step up your efforts  there to stop the flow of migrants and  in boats that are often not suited to  that journey at all where we're seeing  an incredible loss of life at sea well  at present time we have 12 vessels  deployed by Frontex  in our operation on Triton operation in  in Italy between Italy and and Libya we  also have the same number of vessels in  Greece to make sure that there are no  search and rescue case needed there we  have saved lives up to four thousand and  yeah 40,000 40,000 lives were saved last  year by by frontex the problem is when  the migrants are at sea it's too late  because they they put their life at risk  so that there is a need to fix the  problem in cooperation with African  countries and from take is going to  deploy in spring this year  an officer - neow - neow we're going to  post him or her in EMA with the  possibility to cooperate with other EU  actions there the you cap siyul mission  for instance so we are trying now to  have this cooperation on the African  continent in order to save lives because  we also have to think about lives lost  in the desert because everybody's  focused ok what I Mediterranean but  there is a lot of risk in the desert as  well and like to ask you a last brief  question there mr. lazarey and that is  what do you need most right now do you  need diplomatic help or do you need more  naval vessels more people on the ground  in North Africa in desert areas as well  which one's more important right now  from the EU member states to help  Frontex I think to help from text and  and more generally - to help the  European Union to be more efficient in  in tackling this Libyan problem and I  think we need a political input we need  diplomatic efforts in order to really  change the game because the situation in  Libya for instance Frontex contributed  to the training of the Libyan Coast  Guard but of course as long as there is  no let's say effective possibility for  Libyan Coast Guard - - to monitor the  waters or - to carry out border controls  then we are still in in trouble so what  we need right now is something which is  more at political level political  decision in the EU and diplomatic  cooperation with African countries mr.  LaVey thank you so very much for being  with us today thank you for your  comments that was Fabrice Alicia he the  head of front tax that's the European  border and Coast Guard Protection Agency  thank you very much for being with us  thank you very much
 

